# MM_compiler — Web Frontend

# Fateha Jannat Sumaya
# ID: 231-115-215


Paste source code in the browser, hit **COMPILE**, and watch it run through
all 6 backend phases (Lexical → Syntax → Semantic → IR → Optimization →
Target Code) live. Supports all 4 language frontends: C, C++, Java, Python.

```
web/
├── server/     Express backend — spawns the compiled mm_c / mm_cpp / mm_java / mm_python
│               binaries on your submitted source and parses their output into phases.
└── client/     Static frontend — a blueprint/schematic-styled "compilation bench" UI.
                Served automatically by the backend, no build step needed.
```

## 1. Build the compiler binaries first (if not already built)

```bash
cd ../c && make
cd ../cpp && make
cd ../java && make
cd ../python && make
```

## 2. Install & run the web backend

```bash
cd web/server
npm install
npm start
```

Open **http://localhost:4000** — the backend serves the frontend directly.

- Pick a language (C / C++ / Java / Python)
- Write code or load a bundled example (`../<lang>/examples/*`)
- Click **COMPILE** — the **OUTPUT** console shows the program's actual
  printed result (or the compiler error if it failed), like a normal
  compiler run. All 6 phases still run in the backend and are available
  under "Show 6-phase compiler internals" if you want to inspect tokens /
  parse tree / TAC / target code.

## Notes

- Runs each submission through the real Flex/Bison binary (5s timeout, 20k
  char limit). No sandboxing needed — these are toy-language analyzers that
  only print phase output, they don't execute or link real code.
- `server/tacInterpreter.js` is a small interpreter that actually executes
  the optimized three-address code (phase 5) so the OUTPUT console shows
  real computed values (e.g. an actual `10` for a summed loop), not just
  the TAC/assembly text.
- Config lives at the top of `server/server.js` (`LANGS`, `PORT`,
  `RUN_TIMEOUT_MS`, `MAX_SOURCE_CHARS`).
- To serve client separately from backend, set `const API = "http://localhost:4000"`
  at the top of `client/app.js`.
